[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#55FFFF]BeastLib 1.7.4 - GUI Compatibility Fix[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

This update fixes GUI errors affecting BeastTokens and other plugins compiled against older BeastLib versions.

[LIST]
[*]Restores the legacy [B]Player[/B] methods alongside the current [B]HumanEntity[/B] methods for opening and closing menus, including paginated, scrolling and storage menus.
[*]Fixes the [B]NoSuchMethodError: Gui.open(Player)[/B] that could prevent [B]/tokenshop[/B] from opening.
[*]Preserves normal menu behavior and page/close arguments. Existing compiled plugins can continue using their original GUI calls.
[*]Includes the same compatibility methods in the server plugin and developer API artifact.
[/LIST]

[B]Updating:[/B] Stop the server, replace the old BeastLib jar with [B]BeastLib 1.7.4[/B], then start the server. Keep only one BeastLib jar installed. No configuration reset is needed.

For the matching BeastTokens release, install [B]BeastTokens 4.3.15[/B] during the same restart.
